<title>SWEDEN: Bofors wins 200 mln Skr Austrian order.</title>
<headline>Bofors wins 200 mln Skr Austrian order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bofors AB, a unit of Swedish defence group Celsius AB, won an order worth 200 million crowns ($27.7 million) from the Austrian army for the night sight for the BILL anti-tank missile system.</p>
<p>&quot;The first procurement of the BILL was made in 1989. Since then several orders have been placed and more are planned for the future,&quot; the company said in a release.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006 ($ = 7.226 Swedish Crowns)</p>
